sops.workflow:
1. User -> Transportation Planner;
2. Transportation Planner -> Accommodation Planner;
3. Accommodation Planner -> Restaurant Planner and Attractions Planner (in parallel);
4. Restaurant Planner, Attractions Planner -> Final Plan Summarizer;
5. Final Plan Summarizer validates the entire plan against all constraints (including mandatory data fields):
   a. If valid, output final plan and end.
   b. If invalid, send detailed correction request to responsible agent (any prior agent).
6. Responsible agent revises data and sends corrected output directly to Final Plan Summarizer.
7. Return to step 5 for revalidation.

Description:
The Transportation Planner establishes the daily location sequence and transportation framework. Accommodation, Restaurant, and Attractions Planners populate their elements within this framework. The Final Plan Summarizer acts as a gatekeeper: it rigorously validates all inputs against mandatory fields (including self-driving distance), city alignment, uniqueness, and budget. Upon any failure, it triggers targeted revisions with guaranteed response handling, creating a closed validation loop until all constraints are satisfied. This ensures irreversible process halts are eliminated while maintaining parallel processing efficiency.
